ise that never ends. Following Blake's life from beginning to end, acclaimed biographer Leo Damrosch draws extensively on Blake's poems, his paintings, and his etchings and engravings to offer this generously illustrated account of Blake the man and his vision of our world. The author's goal is to inspire the reader with the passion he has for his subject, achieving the imaginative response that Blake himself sought to excite. The book is an invitation to understanding and enjoyment, an invitation to appreciate Blake's imaginative world and, in so doing, to open the doors of our perception.\"--provided by publisher.","publicationYear":2015,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"English Poets","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-eternity-s-sunrise-the-imaginative-world-of-william-blake-leo-damrosch"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-eternity-s-sunrise-the-imaginative-world-of-william-blake-leo-damrosch"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Artists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-eternity-s-sunrise-the-imaginative-world-of-william-blake-leo-damrosch"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Blake, william, 1757-1827","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-eternity-s-sunrise-the-imaginative-world-of-william-blake-leo-damrosch"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Authors, biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-eternity-s-sunrise-the-imaginative-world-of-william-blake-leo-damrosch"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-eternity-s-sunrise-the-imaginative-world-of-william-blake-leo-damrosch"}],"displaySummary":"The author's goal is to inspire the reader with the passion he has for his subject, achieving the imaginative response that Blake h